# shell: desktop
# mount: /devices/board1
# board: only
# A board built without its shell: no prompt, so nothing to mount, but
# the drawing demo's window still rides the console, pumped by the
# kernel's own process.  The desktop finds it on the port alone and the
# window comes up beside the fixture's folder.  This needs the board on
# the cable flashed with TIKU_SHELL_ENABLE=0 TIKU_APPL_GUI=1
# TIKU_APPL_DRAW_DEMO=1; with the shell image on it, the board mounts as
# usual and the window count here is wrong.
wait 30
note the board's window is on the desktop, beside the fixture's folder
expect-windows 2
expect-title Board window
note the button counts: a press crosses to the board and its redraw comes back
click 421 390
wait 45
expect-narrate Pressed 1 time
shot /tmp/trk_boardnoshell.png
quit
